findings.body:
**One zero-length hunk rejects every primary anchor on that side, including anchors that overlap a real changed hunk.**

Line 106 returns `no-hunk-information` when any hunk has `start >= end`. A diff that deletes lines in one place and edits lines in another produces a head-side `[n, n)` hunk and a non-empty head-side hunk. Git reports a pure deletion as a head range of length 0.

In that case a primary anchor inside the edited hunk gets `no-hunk-information`. The evidence is marked invalid even though the quote is exact and the range overlaps a changed line. The check at Line 107 is already correct for non-empty hunks, so ignoring the empty hunks is enough.

If the caller guarantees that it never passes zero-length hunks, this is moot. In that case, remove the check and its test. Otherwise, filter the empty hunks and fail only when none remain.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-    if (hunks.length === 0) return ['no-hunk-information'];
-    if (hunks.some((hunk) => hunk.start >= hunk.end)) return ['no-hunk-information'];
-    const overlaps = hunks.some((hunk) => anchor.start < hunk.end && hunk.start <= anchor.end);
+    const changed = hunks.filter((hunk) => hunk.start < hunk.end);
+    if (changed.length === 0) return ['no-hunk-information'];
+    const overlaps = changed.some((hunk) => anchor.start < hunk.end && hunk.start <= anchor.end);
```

Then update `test/ops/review/findingAnchors.test.ts:597-612`. Use hunks `[{start: 1, end: 2}, {start: 4, end: 4}]`. Assert `valid` for an anchor on line 1, and `outside-changed-hunks` for the line-3 anchor that the test uses now.
</details>
